# ventoy settings: shipped by stack/ventoy. Every setting ventoy reads.
#
# This machine's values go in ~/.config/ventoy/ventoy.local.env, beside this file (yours, never
# shipped). The environment wins over both: `VENTOY_DISK=/dev/sdc ventoy status` does what it says.
# Format: NAME=value, one per line, read and never sourced (only a leading ~/, or a value that is
# ~, is expanded, to $HOME; a value may be quoted). A commented line is the default used when
# nothing sets it. `ventoy config list` shows them and where each is from;
# `ventoy config set NAME=value` writes ventoy.local.env.

# The default disk, e.g. /dev/disk/by-id/usb-... (stable across replugs, unlike /dev/sdX), or a
# disk image, e.g. /srv/nfs/pikvm/ventoy.img; commands without a disk use it (empty: none)
#VENTOY_DISK=
# Size of the disk images `ventoy prepare` creates
#VENTOY_IMAGE_SIZE=64G
# The ISOs that go on the stick: links `ventoy copy <iso>` makes into the store, and any file put
# there by hand (empty: ~/.cache/ventoy/isos)
#VENTOY_ISO_DIR=
